'''Pokémon the Movie 2000''' is a graphic novel published by [[VIZ Media]] in North America and [[Shogakukan]] in Japan. It is a manga-style book (called "Animation Comics" by VIZ at the time of publication, now branded as "Ani-Manga") which retells the plotlines of ''[[M02|The Power of One]]'' and ''[[PK04|Pikachu's Rescue Adventure]]'' using screenshots from both films. The book credits [[Satoshi Tajiri]] and [[Tsunekazu Ishihara]] as the authors.

Like the {{OBP|Pokémon the First Movie|graphic novel}} graphic novel, ''Pokémon the Movie 2000'' was originally published in Japan as simply one bound volume. For the North American release, it was split up into five monthly issues: four for ''The Power of One'' and one for ''Pikachu's Rescue Adventure''. After the release of the monthly issues, the story was rereleased as one bound volume.

The ''Pikachu's Rescue Adventure'' chapter was later reprinted in the [[All That Pikachu!]] graphic novel.

